---
description: Rules for Steam Online Subsystem (OSS) integration, session handling, matchmaking, and Steam P2P multiplayer logic.
globs: Source/**/*GameInstance*, Source/**/*Session*, Source/**/*Online*, Source/**/*.h, Source/**/*.cpp
alwaysApply: false
---

- ALWAYS use `IOnlineSubsystem::Get(STEAM_SUBSYSTEM)` for session handling, matchmaking, and player identity.
- Use `IOnlineSessionPtr` interface for creating, searching, and joining Steam Lobbies.
- Ensure multiplayer connection strings utilize Steam P2P / Unique Net IDs when connecting clients to the host.
- Wrap Steam-specific code safely with `#if WITH_STEAM` checks where appropriate or ensure Fallback to `NULL` subsystem for offline testing.